<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore May non-oil exports fall 1.0 pct on yr.</title>
<headline>Singapore May non-oil exports fall 1.0 pct on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 1.0 pct percent year-on-year in May compared to the same month in the previous year, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Friday.  </p>
<p>In nominal terms, non-oil exports fell to Singapore S$7.42 billion.</p>
<p>TDB said the decline was less severe than the 4.1 percent contraction in the first quarter of 1997. April and May data taken together showed non-oil domestic exports increased by 2.4 percent compared to the corresponding two months last year.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 10 Singapore-based economists had predicted a nominal year-on-year rise of 3.5 percent in May.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports rose 0.5 percent in May to S$9.57 billion after rising an adjusted 8.2 percent in April.  </p>
